# RESEARCH PROCESS

All research shall follow a structured lifecycle.

```text id="801res01"
Problem Identification
        │
        ▼
Hypothesis Formation
        │
        ▼
Information Gathering
        │
        ▼
Analysis
        │
        ▼
Evaluation
        │
        ▼
Documentation
        │
        ▼
Recommendation
```

Each stage must produce traceable output.

---

# RESEARCH OUTPUTS

Research may produce:

* technical evaluations
* architectural proposals
* system improvement recommendations
* experimental designs
* feasibility studies
* comparative analyses
* risk assessments

All outputs remain non-binding until validated.

---

# VALIDATION REQUIREMENT

Research findings must pass through:

* Series 704 Testing (where applicable)
* Series 705 Validation (if advanced toward implementation)
* Governance review (Series 000)
* Architectural alignment (Series 200)

Research alone does not authorize implementation.

---

# EVIDENCE REQUIREMENT

All research conclusions must be supported by:

* documented sources
* experimental data
* system measurements
* comparative analysis
* or clearly stated assumptions

Unsupported claims are not valid research outputs.

---

# KNOWLEDGE INTEGRATION

Validated research may be integrated into:

* system architecture updates
* engine improvements
* interface enhancements
* workflow optimizations
* future system designs (Series 800+ evolution paths)

Integration must follow governed deployment processes.

---

# VERSIONING

Research outputs must include:

* version history
* research date
* contributor or system agent
* scope definition
* assumptions and limitations

This ensures reproducibility and traceability.

---

# GOVERNANCE

Research shall never:

* directly modify production systems
* bypass validation requirements
* introduce untested changes into live environments
* conceal uncertainty or limitations
* present hypotheses as production facts

Research exists to inform decisions, not execute them.

---

